  "domain": "blockchain",
  "definition": "BIP-341 is the Bitcoin Improvement Proposal that specifies the Taproot upgrade, introducing Pay-to-Taproot (P2TR) as a native SegWit version 1 output type that unifies key-path and script-path spending under a single Schnorr-based commitment. It integrates Merklised Alternative Script Trees (MAST) so that only the executed spending branch is revealed on-chain, preserving the privacy of unexplored script conditions. BIP-341 activated on the Bitcoin mainnet at block 709,632 in November 2021 via the Speedy Trial soft-fork mechanism, requiring 90% miner signalling. It forms part of the Taproot bundle alongside BIP-340 (Schnorr signatures for Bitcoin) and BIP-342 (Tapscript), collectively the largest upgrade to Bitcoin's scripting system since SegWit.",
